    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup led by **Yordan Alvarez** (85.52) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13). **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from an elite xwOBA of 0.477 and a favorable matchup against Young, whose xERA of 4.66 creates a prime environment for production. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** serves as our primary engine for the stolen base category; his 100% stolen base rate against a slow-delivering Matthews, combined with the leadoff spot, makes him a foundational piece. We are also looking for a significant output from **Junior Caminero** (70.19) and **Colt Keith** (69.64). **Junior Caminero** leverages a strong park factor and a positive platoon edge against Gray, while **Colt Keith** is positioned perfectly to capitalize on the 4.87 xERA of Ryan Johnson, assuming the projected #3 spot holds.\n\nRegarding roster management, the most difficult decision involved **Carson Benge** (51.46). While his platoon advantage and park factors were favorable, he ultimately fell short of the starting threshold because his base efficiency projection could not overcome the higher scoring potential of **Lars Nootbaar** and **Kyle Schwarber**, even with **Lars Nootbaar** facing a minor dynamic platoon penalty against Eduardo Rodriguez. Managers should note that the lineups for **Dillon Dingler**, **Colt Keith**, **Nelson Velazquez**, and **Lars Nootbaar** remain pending as of this report. **Trea Turner** (56.61) and **Kyle Schwarber** (55.17) both face the tough arm of McLean, which suppresses their scoring potential relative to our top-tier options; however, their power profile necessitates their inclusion in the active lineup. We are avoiding **Jacob Gonzalez** (40.00) today, as his platoon disadvantage against Cantillo renders him below our efficiency floor.",
